        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Approached via a long, winding driveway, this striking two-storey, brick-fronted residence enjoys an enviable setting on c. 1.26 acres (0.51 hectares) of beautifully mature grounds. Architecturally designed with a distinctive and thoughtfully planned layout, the home offers a unique living experience, with the principal living room positioned on the first floor to maximise its breath taking surroundings. Flooded with natural light through expansive picture windows, this elegant space frames uninterrupted views of the mature woodland, rolling hills and tranquil lake beyond, creating a truly exceptional setting for both everyday living and entertaining. The spacious kitchen and dining room with cosy Rayburn and AGA range cooker is positioned to the rear of the property, where patio doors open onto a sun-drenched terrace, perfectly placed to enjoy the spectacular views and peaceful setting. Designed with both practicality and family living in mind, the kitchen is further enhanced by a generous walk-in pantry and a large utility room. The accommodation comprises four well-proportioned bedrooms arranged over two floors, including the master bedroom with en-suite bathroom. A stylish family bathroom and a separate study, ideal for working from home, complete the well-balanced accommodation, extending to approximately 169 sq. mts.\r\nThe grounds surrounding the property are every gardener's dream. Beautifully landscaped lawns, mature specimen trees and colourful shrubbery create a private yet colourful and picturesque setting throughout the site. A large paddock to the side of the property offers excellent potential for hobby farming, equestrian use or simply additional recreational space. A selection of outbuildings and storage sheds further enhance the property's versatility, providing endless possibilities for workshops, storage, gardening, or a variety of other uses.\r\nCombining distinctive architecture, generous living accommodation, exceptional privacy and breath taking natural surroundings, this is a truly unique home offering an outstanding lifestyle opportunity.\r\n\r\nLOCATION\r\nThis property is beautifully located within walking distance of the picturesque and popular village of Ballymore Eustace in Co. Kildare. The property lies in an enviable position overlooking the Goldenfalls lake and ski club with access via a quiet country lane.  Ballymore Eustace is a peaceful rural village, with a great sense of community yet within easy access of major road networks including the M7 and N81. It has award winning pubs and restaurants, a school, shops and a thriving GAA club. It is just 15 kms from Naas and 11 kms from Blessington, each with an abundance of shops, restaurants, bars, sporting facilities and secondary schools. The village has an ever-increasing population and has proven to be a very popular and exclusive location with its rural feel yet it's close proximity to Naas town and the City. The Ballymore Eustace loop is a delightful c. 5km walk along the River Liffey which is popular with residents of the locality. This walk passes close to the house and is an amazing amenity to have on your doorstep. The Village of Ballymore Eustace has new addition of transport with the local link leaving the Village 6 times a day with stops to Blessington, Naas and Sallins train station. Dublin bus number 65 also in service right into Dublin City centre.\r\n\r\nFEATURES\r\n•\tLarge sweeping drive.\r\n•\tAmple parking.\r\n•\tLands c. 1.26 acres / 0.51 HA.\r\n•\tLarge paddock.\r\n•\tCar port.\r\n•\tDetached wooden shed.\r\n•\tGreenhouse.\r\n•\tPatio area.\r\n•\tViews of Goldenfalls Lake. \r\n•\tWater: Mains.\r\n•\tSewage: Septic tank.\r\n•\tHeating: Dual central heating Oil & Solid Fuel."
      },
